[h1]Flavorium Universalis — v0.3.7 Hotfix[/h1]

[i]Compatible with EU5 1.3.* BETA | Multiplayer synchronized[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]New: Frontier Governance[/h2]

A lesser governor for the lands roads and cities never reach — helping realms that push into the steppe, the mountains, and the deep interior hold their gains.

[list]
[*] [b]Frontier Governor[/b] building — a resident noble administrator buildable in [b]rural[/b], non-road-connected provinces, so long as they remain connected to the capital by land (directly or through subjects). Projects less proximity than a full Local Governor and draws from its own small pool.
[*] [b]Frontier Administration[/b] advance (branch-independent, Age of Renaissance) — unlocks the building and the frontier estate privileges, and grants the first governor slot. AI research is biased toward frontier-prone realms (Eastern Europe, the steppe, Anatolia/the Near-East, East Asia) and toward Muscovy, Novgorod, the Ottomans, and the holder of the Mandate of Heaven.
[*] [b]Frontier estate privileges[/b] — each estate can specialize the governor's surrounding provinces: [b]Governance[/b] (nobles, an extra governor slot + local control), [b]Missions[/b] (clergy, faster conversion to the state religion), [b]Markets[/b] (burghers, market access and trade), and [b]Settlement[/b] (peasants, migration and pop promotion). Bonuses refresh yearly and fade if the governor or privilege is lost.
[/list]
